; Button's composite paint: a StyleBox under a text run, per draw state.
;
; The one variable: what a Button assembles for itself. Six buttons of the SAME
; 300x72 rect on the same grid, differing only in the fields that pick or
; suppress a piece of that assembly — so a missing layer, a wrong stylebox or a
; mis-placed glyph run can only be the painter.
;
; Normal is the control: the default theme's `normal` box under centred text.
; Disabled changes only `disabled = true`, which swaps BOTH layers at once —
; the `disabled` stylebox (the same fill at half alpha, so it reads as a
; fainter plate against the same backdrop) and `font_disabled_color` over the
; text. Two layers is the point: a painter that dimmed only the box, or only
; the glyphs, still produces a believable "disabled" button, and this is the
; only pane where those two can be told apart.
;
; Themed replaces `theme_override_styles/normal` with a box whose fill, corner
; radii and content margins are all authored away from the theme's. Flat sets
; `flat = true`, which suppresses the box entirely and leaves the glyph run
; alone over the backdrop — the one pane that proves the text is a layer of its
; own rather than something baked into the plate.
;
; Left and Right carry the SAME authored box as Themed and differ from it only
; in `alignment`. The box has a 24 px horizontal content margin, so the two
; place their glyph runs against that inset rather than against the raw rect
; edge; a painter that aligned to the rect would sit 24 px out on both, in
; opposite directions, while the centred panes above stayed perfect.
;
; No other golden draws a Button, a themed widget stylebox, or a disabled
; state, so all of the above is unguarded elsewhere.
;
; Measured against Godot 4.6.3 at `--mode 2d`: every plate colour is exact —
; rgb(28, 29, 32) for `normal` over this backdrop, rgb(30, 31, 37) for
; `disabled`, rgb(51, 128, 89) for the authored box, and the backdrop itself
; where Flat draws no box at all. Each pane's glyph run sits within one pixel of
; the engine's in both axes, Left's at x 745 and Right's ending at x 994 —
; i.e. inset by the authored 24 px content margin on both sides, not by the rect
; edge. What remains is stem antialiasing from the MSDF atlas, about 300 px per
; pane, and it is confined to the button rects: the backdrop matches exactly.

